Language research centers on comprehension, structural grammar, oral traditions, and expressive literature in English, Shona, and Ndebele.
• Proverb (Tsumo / Izaga): A wise, brief traditional saying that conveys a deep life lesson, moral truth, or cultural warning using figurative language.
• Idiom (Madimikira / Izitsho): A cultural expression whose true meaning cannot be understood from the literal definitions of the individual words.
• Ngano / Inganekwane: Traditional fireside folktales told orally by elders to children to pass down historical morals, usually featuring talking animals (e.g., Tsuro the clever hare).
