• Endocrine Gland: A ductless gland that manufactures specific hormone molecules and secretes them directly into the bloodstream to regulate distant target organs.
• Endothermic Reaction: A chemical transformation that absorbs thermal energy from its immediate surroundings, causing the temperature of the system to drop.
• Endurance: The physical stamina to keep exercising or playing a sport for a long time without getting overly tired.
