• Enthalpy: The total heat content or thermal energy stored within a thermodynamic system at constant pressure.
• Enzyme: A biological catalyst composed of protein that accelerates metabolic chemical reactions inside organisms without being consumed.
• Epicenter: The point on the Earth's surface directly above the focus or origin point of an earthquake.
• Ecosystem: A community where living organisms interact directly with non-living elements and weather patterns.
• Equilibrium: A stable state in which opposing forces, influences, or chemical reaction rates are perfectly balanced.
• Equinox: The two times each year when the sun crosses the celestial equator, resulting in day and night being of approximately equal length all over the earth.
