Section G

• Game Reserve: A large area of wild land set aside specifically for protecting and breeding wild animals.
• Gateway: A network hardware device or software node that connects two distinct networks utilizing different communication protocols.
• Gene: A specific unit of heredity made up of a DNA sequence that carries instructions for building proteins and passing on traits.
