• Glacier: A massive, slow-moving river of ice formed by the accumulation and compaction of snow over centuries.
• Global Warming: The long-term rise in Earth's temperature caused by greenhouse gases trapping heat in the atmosphere.
• Glucose: A simple sugar molecule that serves as an essential source of metabolic energy for living organisms during cellular respiration.
• Gradient: A numeric measure of the steepness, incline, or rate of vertical rise relative to horizontal run of a straight line or curve.
