• Lightning: [Physics / Combined Science] A massive natural electrostatic discharge occurring between a cloud and the ground, or between clouds, creating an intense electrical path.
• Lime: [Building Technology / Agriculture] Calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (hydrated lime), processed for structural mortar or added to agricultural fields to neutralize acidic soil.
• Limited Liability: [Commerce] A legal condition where shareholders' financial losses in a company are strictly capped at the amount they invested in shares, protecting personal assets.
• Limiting Factor: [Advanced Biology / Combined Science] An environmental variable or resource—such as light intensity, temperature, or carbon dioxide concentration—that restricts the rate of a biological process.
• Limpopo River: [Combined Science / Geography] The major river forming Zimbabwe's southern boundary with South Africa, flowing through dry Lowveld ecosystems.
• Linear Equation: [Advanced Mathematics] An algebraic equation of the first degree that forms a perfectly straight line when plotted on a coordinate graph.
• Lintel: [Building Technology] A horizontal structural beam constructed from timber, stone, reinforced concrete, or steel spanning the top of a door or window opening to support masonry loads above.
• Lipase: [Advanced Biology / Combined Science] A digestive enzyme secreted by the pancreas and intestinal glands that breaks down lipid molecules into fatty acids and glycerol.
• Lipid: [Chemistry / Advanced Biology] A broad group of organic molecules insoluble in water but soluble in organic solvents, comprising fats, oils, waxes, and phospholipids, acting as membrane components and energy stores.
• Liquid: [Physics / Chemistry] A fundamental state of matter where particles possess intermediate kinetic energy and are free to move past one another, maintaining a definite volume but taking the shape of their container.
• Litmus: [Chemistry / Combined Science] A water-soluble mixture of organic dyes extracted from lichens, used as a baseline chemical indicator that turns red in acidic solutions and blue in alkaline solutions.
• Liturgical Rituals: [Family & Religious Studies] Structured, public religious practices, prayers, or patterns of worship performed by a faith community according to established ecclesiastical traditions.
• Liver: [Advanced Biology] A large metabolic organ in vertebrates responsible for detoxifying blood plasma, synthesizing proteins, regulating glucose levels, and producing bile.
• Livestock: [Combined Science / Agriculture] Domesticated animals, such as cattle, goats, sheep, and poultry, raised on farms for food, labor, or income.
• Load-Bearing Wall: [Building Technology] An exterior or interior wall designed to support vertical structural loads from roofs, floors, and upper walls in addition to its own weight.
