• Locus: [Advanced Mathematics] A set or configuration of points whose coordinates satisfy a specific mathematical rule or geometric condition.
• Logarithm: [Advanced Mathematics] The mathematical exponent or power to which a fixed base number must be raised to yield a given value.
• Longitudinal Wave: [Physics] A wave pattern where the physical displacement or oscillation of the medium is parallel to the direction of wave energy propagation (e.g., sound waves).
• Long-sightedness / Hypermetropia: [Physics / Combined Science] A vision defect where light rays focus behind the retina instead of directly on it, making close objects look blurry while distant objects are clear.
