• Luminescence: [Physics] The emission of light by a substance not resulting from heat, occurring via chemical reactions, electrical energy, or subatomic motion.
• Lungs: [Advanced Biology / Combined Science] A pair of vascular respiratory organs in terrestrial vertebrates responsible for exchanging oxygen and carbon dioxide between blood and air.
