• Lymphocyte: [Advanced Biology] A specialized type of white blood cell (B cells and T cells) responsible for coordinating the adaptive immune response against specific pathogens.
• Lysosome: [Advanced Biology] A membrane-bound cellular organelle containing hydrolytic enzymes responsible for breaking down waste materials, cellular debris, and foreign invaders.

