• Non-biodegradable: [Combined Science] Tough synthetic matter or chemical materials—such as plastic bottles, glass, and heavy metals—that cannot be broken down naturally by decomposers over time, causing environmental pollution.
• Non-Electrolyte: [Chemistry] A liquid substance or chemical compound that does not dissociate into ions in solution and is completely incapable of conducting an electric current.
• Non-Metal: [Chemistry] A class of chemical elements characterized by poor electrical and thermal conductivity, brittle solid states, lack of metallic luster, and a high electronegativity to gain electrons.
• Non-Reducing Sugar: [Chemistry / Combined Science] A carbohydrate sugar, most notably sucrose, that lacks a free aldehyde or ketone group, meaning it cannot reduce copper(II) ions in Fehling's or Benedict's solution without prior acid hydrolysis.
• Non-Ruminant: [Combined Science / Agriculture] An animal with a simple, single-compartment stomach system (such as pigs, horses, and poultry) that cannot digest cellulose via standard rumination.
• Normal Distribution: [Advanced Mathematics] A continuous, completely symmetrical bell-shaped probability distribution centered around its mean, widely used in statistical data analysis.
• Nosing: [Building Technology] The rounded, projecting front edge of a stair tread extending outward over the vertical riser below to provide a larger stepping surface and improve safety.
• Notochord: [Advanced Biology] A flexible, rod-like longitudinal structural skeletal element running along the dorsal side of all chordate embryos, providing support, later replaced by the vertebral column in vertebrates.
• Noun: [Languages] A fundamental part of speech that names a specific person, place, physical object, or abstract concept.
• Noun Classes: [Languages] The systematic grammatical grouping system in Bantu languages (like Shona and Ndebele) that categorizes nouns into different classes based on their singular and plural structural prefixes.
• Noxious Weed: [Agriculture] An invasive, highly competitive, or toxic weed species designated by agricultural regulations as harmful to crops, livestock, or native ecosystems.
