• Open Circuit: [Physics] An electrical circuit path that is broken or interrupted, preventing the continuous flow of electric current.
• Open-Hearth Process: [Chemistry / Metallurgical Engineering] An old industrial method used to refine steel from pig iron by burning off excess carbon and impurities inside a shallow furnace using preheated air.
