• Orthogonal: [Advanced Mathematics / Physics] A geometric condition where two vectors, lines, or planes are completely perpendicular to each other, intersecting at an angle of 90 degrees.
• Orthographic Projection: [Technical Graphics / Design & Technology] A standardized drafting method used to represent a three-dimensional object by projecting flat, two-dimensional views (front, top, side) onto planes at right angles.
